    "ver": "0.31.0",
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "## MiniMax H3 (universal multi-reference to video)\n\nOmni-modal video model: up to 15s of 24fps video with native stereo audio\n(dialog in 11 languages). Requires ComfyUI 0.30.0+ and the Ref2VA checkpoint.\n\nThis graph carries EVERY reference loader the app can wire:\n\n- `<AITOOLS_INPUT_1>` reference clip 1 -> `ref_videos.ref_video_0` (+ soundtrack)\n- `<AITOOLS_INPUT_2>` reference clip 2 -> `ref_videos.ref_video_1` (+ soundtrack)\n- `<AITOOLS_INPUT_3>`..`_11` reference photos 1-9 -> `ref_images.ref_image_0..8`\n\nSeth's AI Tools PRUNES unused loaders at submit time: any loader whose\n`<AITOOLS_INPUT_N>` placeholder is still unfilled is removed from the\nAPI-format JSON (references cascade-removed, autogrow indices renumbered),\nand a silent clip's audio wire is dropped via `@prune_input`. To run this\ngraph manually in ComfyUI, delete the loaders you aren't using and fill real\npaths into the rest.\n\nPrompt tags are per-type in connection order among the references that\nREMAIN: clips are `<Video 1>` / `<Video 2>`, their soundtracks `<Audio 1>` /\n`<Audio 2>`, photos are `<Picture 1>`..`<Picture 9>`. Give each reference ONE\njob (e.g. `<Video 1>` = motion/camera/voice, `<Picture 1>` = person identity).\n\n`length` is a frame count at 24fps, snapped up to the model's 17k+5 grid\n(124 = ~5s, trained range is ~124-362 = ~5-15s). Canvas max is 768x1344-area\n(~1MP); this workflow defaults to 864x480 (~0.4MP, the official template\ndefault).\n\nThe `MiniMaxH3MemoryEfficientSageAttentionPatch` node (kjnodes) needs the\n`sageattention` pip package on the server; delete or bypass it to run without.\n\n**Models** (from [Comfy-Org/MiniMax-H3](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MiniMax-H3)):\n\n- `diffusion_models/minimax_h3_ref2va_pruned_int8_convrot.safetensors`\n- `text_encoders/qwen3vl_32b_minimax_h3_nvfp4_awq.safetensors`\n- `vae/minimax_h3_video_vae_fp16.safetensors`\n- `vae/minimax_h3_audio_vae_fp32.safetensors`\n"
   ],
   "title": "About this workflow"
  },
